{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And he defiled the head of his naziriteship.</b> The vav of addition says, and it also says the word <b>head</b>, to convey that even though it is only an impurity of inadvertence, nevertheless not only did his body become impure, but even the sanctity that is upon his head, as it is written: ״נֵזֶר אֱלֹהָיו עַל רֹאשׁוֹ״." "It further intends to say that he did not suspend the naziriteship from that point onward alone, but rather <b>and he defiled</b> also the head of his naziriteship — meaning, the beginning of the naziriteship. This is what Scripture concludes: <b>he shall consecrate to HaShem</b>, etc., <b>and the first days shall fall.</b> And the reason it repeated afterward <b>for his naziriteship is impure</b>, and did not suffice with what preceded in the statement ״and he defiled the head of his naziriteship,״ is so there be no opening for a litigant to argue that only one day became impure — namely the beginning of the naziriteship — and the statement <b>and the first days</b> revealed that not one day alone from the beginning of the naziriteship becomes impure, but rather the two first ones and not all the days; and it is a decree of Scripture — Scripture says to say ״for his naziriteship is impure״ in a general manner."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:21.561943450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}